# Planning + reference docs — NEVER commit (public repo; real names and
# security findings live in these). Listed one-by-one until 7 Aug 2026, which
# meant every NEW doc was unprotected by default until someone remembered to
# add it. IOS_SUBMISSION.md was sitting untracked-but-committable when this was
# noticed. Blanket rule instead: zero .md files are tracked in this repo, so
# nothing breaks, and a new doc is safe the moment it is created.
*.md
SOLO_ROADMAP.md
AUTH_WEEKEND_ROADMAP.md

# Firebase Functions deps (installed via npm, never committed)
functions/node_modules/
node_modules/

# Firebase emulator debug logs
*-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log
firebase-debug.log

# Security model — deployed via `firebase deploy --only firestore:rules` from
# the LOCAL copy. Untracked because GitHub Pages serves every tracked file at
# the site root: goforge.in/firestore.rules returned 200, handing anyone a map
# of exactly what the rules do and do not allow. Removing it is PROSPECTIVE
# only — 15 revisions are already public and must be assumed known. Canonical
# copy + backups live in ~/Desktop/forge-backups/.
firestore.rules
